[medium, design] gix-store/src/index.rs:10-22 — the cache namespace ignores Layout. index::reference hardcodes refs/cache/<kind-hex>/index-v1, while entity and schema refs are namespaced by the caller's Layout (store.rs:19-24). Two stores opened over the same repo with different Layouts and the same kind name share one index ref: each writer's index is stale from the other's perspective, so they perpetually invalidate and overwrite each other's cache and force spurious LostRace retries on every write (the read-side equality check keeps this *correct*, but the cache thrashes forever). Worse, an adversarial-but-legal Layout of data = refs/cache with a kind named k<hex> makes an entity ref collide with the index ref itself. The cache ref should be derived from the Layout (as the recent namespacing commit did for kind), or Layout should carry a cache prefix.
